<Sequence DisplayName="HMS Client" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_11">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>shared/HMS_Client.xaml — reusable wrapper around the Mock HMS REST API (docs/phase1/hms_interfaces.md Part B and D).</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<Sequence DisplayName="1. Build request" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_2">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Every HMS API call from every bot goes through this one workflow, so auth,
retry and error handling are written exactly once.

The API key arrives as a SecureString from the HMS_ApiKey credential asset.
Convert it only at the moment of the call and never log it — project.json
excludes *apikey* and *token* from logged data for the same reason.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text='TODO(Studio): URL = in_BaseUrl.TrimEnd("/") &amp; "/api/v1" &amp; in_Path ; header X-API-Key from in_ApiKey' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_1" />
</Sequence>
<TryCatch DisplayName="2. Call with retry" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_7">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Retry ONLY when the response says so. The HMS returns one envelope for every error:
  {"error_code": "SLOT_TAKEN", "message": "...", "retryable": true}

Branch on error_code and retryable. Never parse the message text.

  2xx                       success, out_ErrorCode = ""
  retryable = true          wait 2s, 4s, 8s and retry, up to in_MaxAttempts
                            (INTERNAL_ERROR, and network timeouts)
  SLOT_TAKEN / SLOT_LOCKED  retryable, but return immediately — the CALLER
                            retries with a different slot; hammering the same
                            slot would never succeed
  retryable = false         return at once with out_ErrorCode set
  401 UNAUTHORIZED          throw a system exception: the asset is wrong and
                            every following call will fail the same way

Render's free tier cold-starts after 15 idle minutes, so the first call of a
run can take 30+ seconds. That is why the timeout is 30s and a timeout counts
as retryable.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
